          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="N42kKp3f802c-h-2Ez8b-29" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Claim&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Voting to deny just compensation is a municipal policy for fish amendment violation&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Facts:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="430" x="1300" y="610" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="N42kKp3f802c-h-2Ez8b-30" edge="1" parent="1" source="N42kKp3f802c-h-2Ez8b-32" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" target="N42kKp3f802c-h-2Ez8b-11">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="N42kKp3f802c-h-2Ez8b-31" edge="1" parent="1" source="N42kKp3f802c-h-2Ez8b-32" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" target="N42kKp3f802c-h-2Ez8b-15">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="N42kKp3f802c-h-2Ez8b-32" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Defense&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;There was no municipal policy to raid the wrong home, and the City cannot be held liable under a vicarious liability (respondeat superior) theory [JA 28, 32].&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Not simply respondeat superior, but also negligence for not clear instructions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Facts:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="430" x="1770" y="610" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="7IDDNNIT2U_FWAsyabvV" name="Page-3">
    <mxGraphModel dx="3830" dy="2763" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-2" edge="1" parent="1" source="vPt7_FUP9xOXfKO9OSvj-1" style="rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-26" edge="1" parent="1" source="vPt7_FUP9xOXfKO9OSvj-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-25" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vPt7_FUP9xOXfKO9OSvj-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Fifth Amendment Inverse Condemnation&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;The Claim: The SWAT team&#39;s physical destruction of the Nguyens&#39; home ($112,678 in damages) to execute a warrant was a public &quot;taking&quot; of private property for public use, requiring &quot;just compensation&quot; under the Fifth Amendment [JA 3]. The Defense: Tactical law enforcement damage is a non-compensable exercise of the state&#39;s emergency Police Power (or necessity), which operates as an exception to the Takings Clause [JA 9, 26, 32].&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Nguyens owned 3600 White Oaks Drive; the warrant identified Patterson at 3603, across the street. [JA 18–20]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;SWAT forced entry and deployed tear gas; doors, windows, the garage door, and fence were damaged. Remediation and repairs cost $112,678 and took almost 90 days. [JA 16, 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Council denied their property-damage claim; insurance also denied coverage. [JA 23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="390" width="550" x="2783.0" y="-138.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vPt7_FUP9xOXfKO9OSvj-2" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Municipal Liability &amp;amp; Section 1983 Policy/Custom&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;The Claim: Mission City is liable under § 1983 because its City Council—the final policymaking body—voted to deny the Nguyens just compensation, thereby officially executing the municipal policy that completed the Fifth Amendment violation [JA 3–4, 28]. The Defense: There was no municipal policy to raid the wrong home, and the City cannot be held liable under a vicarious liability (respondeat superior) theory [JA 28, 32].&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Mission City is a municipal public corporation governed by a five-member Council empowered to make official City decisions; defendants admit these facts. [JA 1 ¶3; JA 7 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Nguyens filed their claim April 14, 2025. A May 24 letter reported that the Council voted to deny it. [JA 23 ¶14]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;This vote supports plaintiffs’ official-decision theory; the City argues there was no policy authorizing entry into the wrong house. [JA 28–29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="390" width="550" x="2691.0" y="-736.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-4" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-3" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-14" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-13" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-16" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-15" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-24" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-23" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Is Mission City a person who, under color of any statute, ordinance, regulation, custom, or usage, of any State, subjected, or caused to be subjected, a citizen of the United States to the deprivation of any rights, privileges, or immunities secured by the Constitution and laws? Is P a party injured? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Mission City’s own SWAT officers entered and damaged the Nguyens’ home while executing an arrest warrant. [JA 12–16, 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Nguyens are U.S. citizens (admitted); repairs cost $112,678; the Council voted to deny their claim. [JA 1, 7, 23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;These facts support the elements; whether there was a taking and a causative municipal policy remains disputed. [JA 27–29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="550" x="2185.0" y="690.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-6" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-3" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-5" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-8" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-3" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-7" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-12" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-3" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-11" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-3" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Is Mission City a person who&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Mission City is a municipal public corporation organized under Columbia law, with capacity to sue and be sued. [JA 1 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Defendants expressly admit paragraph 3. [JA 7 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="550" x="874.0" y="1541.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-5" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;How have courts interpreted “person” in the Section 1983 context?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Relevant classification fact: Mission City is a municipal corporation, governed by its own five-member City Council. Defendants admit this status. [JA 1 ¶3; JA 7 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;How “person” is interpreted is a legal question; these facts establish the kind of defendant to which the rule would apply.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="550" x="-575.0" y="2185.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-10" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-7" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-9" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-7" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;When does municipal liability attach under Section 1983?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Council has authority to make official City decisions. [JA 1 ¶3; admitted JA 7 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Council itself voted to deny the Nguyens’ submitted property-damage claim. [JA 23 ¶14]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Plaintiffs rely on this single official decision; the City disputes its causal connection to the alleged taking. [JA 28–29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="550" x="483.0" y="2185.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-9" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Under what circumstances may a property owner sue a municipality for just compensation when municipal police damage private property?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Owners’ home was forcibly entered by City SWAT; tear gas made it temporarily uninhabitable and required HAZMAT remediation. [JA 19, 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Repairs cost $112,678; insurance denied coverage and the Council denied their City claim. [JA 23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;These facts support uncompensated loss; whether police damage qualifies as a taking remains a legal dispute. [JA 27–28]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="550" x="161.0" y="2691.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-11" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Is this a situation where courts would extend liability to municipalities?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The denial came from the Council itself, not merely an individual officer: its vote was reported in the City’s May 24, 2025 letter. [JA 23 ¶14]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Council’s official-decision authority is admitted. [JA 1 ¶3; JA 7 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Supports plaintiffs’ theory of direct municipal action; it does not establish a City policy to raid wrong addresses. [JA 28–29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="550" x="1518.0" y="2185.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-13" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Was Mission City acting under the color of a statute, ordinance, regulation, custom, or usage of a State? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The police chief assigned Quick to execute a state arrest warrant. Quick commanded the City SWAT team and planned its deployment. [JA 12–15, 17]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;City officers carried out that operation, and the City Council later voted on the owners’ claim. [JA 16, 23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;These were exercises of governmental authority, supporting the under-color-of-law element.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="550" x="2001.0" y="1725.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-18" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-15" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-17" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-22" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-15" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-21" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-15" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;If yes, in such action, did Mission City subject, or cause to be subjected, P to the deprivation of any rights, privileges, or immunities secured by the Constitution and laws? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;City SWAT breached the home, deployed tear gas, and damaged property; the Council later denied the owners’ claim. [JA 16, 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The resulting repairs cost $112,678. [JA 23 ¶13]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Supports plaintiffs’ claimed uncompensated deprivation; whether these acts violate the Fifth Amendment is contested. [JA 27–29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="550" x="3128.0" y="1564.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-20" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-17" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-19" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-17" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Did such action subject P to the deprivation of their 5th Amendment rights? In other words, did P have their private property taken for public use, without just compensation? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Private property: Kevin and Cindy owned the home. [JA 19 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Public-purpose argument: City SWAT used the home in an operation intended to arrest a suspected fentanyl dealer. [JA 13, 15–16]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Uncompensated loss: $112,678 in repairs; Council voted to deny the claim. These support the taking theory, not a finding that a taking occurred. [JA 23; JA 27–28]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="550" x="2921.0" y="2093.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-19" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;See Issue 2. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Issue 2 facts: forced entry at 3600 although the warrant identified 3603; tear gas and damage to doors, windows, fence, and garage. [JA 16, 18, 22]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Home temporarily uninhabitable; HAZMAT remediation; repairs took almost 90 days and cost $112,678; Council denied claim. [JA 23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Apply Issue 2’s taking analysis to these facts.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="550" x="2852.0" y="2553.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-21" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Was Mission City the one subjecting or causing to be subjected? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;City SWAT physically caused the damage; Quick admits the team entered the wrong house. [JA 16; JA 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Council itself voted to deny compensation. [JA 23 ¶14]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Plaintiffs connect that official denial to the unpaid taking; the City argues the later vote did not cause the original injury. [JA 28–29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="550" x="3956.0" y="2093.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-23" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Is P a citizen of the United States?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Kevin and Cindy allege they are U.S. citizens, married, and Columbia residents. [JA 1 ¶1]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Both defendants expressly admit paragraph 1. Citizenship is therefore admitted in the pleadings. [JA 7 ¶1]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="550" x="3542.0" y="1127.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-25" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;What relief is appropriate?&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Repair-cost evidence: $112,678, with almost 90 days of repairs and HAZMAT remediation. [JA 23 ¶¶12–13]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Requested relief: just compensation on Count II; damages according to proof, costs, and reasonable attorney’s fees on Count III. [JA 5]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The repair total supports the requested amount; it does not itself decide the legally recoverable measure.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="420" x="3381.0" y="713.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-30" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-27" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-29" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-32" edge="1" parent="1" source="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-27" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-31" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-27" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Unjust Enrichment claim&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Officers entered and used the wrong home during the warrant operation, causing physical damage. [JA 16, 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Plaintiffs allege entry without consent, payment, or contract, and no intent to confer a gift. [JA 4 ¶¶21–24]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Claimed benefit: use/access without paying. This is plaintiffs’ theory; the City denies any recognizable benefit. [JA 29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="420" x="5014.0" y="-437.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-29" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Is there any historical basis for recognizing this claim?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Factual analogy to trespass: Quick admits mistaken entry; officers forced entry and damaged the home. [JA 16, 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Plaintiffs allege no consent and no gift. [JA 4 ¶¶21–24]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Historical recognition needs legal authority, not case facts. Counsel invoked older federal restitution cases and the Restatement, but that argument is not a holding. [JA 29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="420" x="4600.0" y="69.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-31" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;What relief is appropriate?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Plaintiffs request money equal to the cost of restoring the property to its pre-raid condition. [JA 5, prayer ¶4]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Kevin reports $112,678 in repairs, including remediation after tear gas made the home temporarily uninhabitable. [JA 23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;This proves claimed loss, not the value of the City’s alleged benefit; restitution’s proper measure remains to be established.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="420" x="5382.0" y="46.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="page3-similar-cases-20260927" name="Page-3 — Similar Cases">
    <mxGraphModel dx="3830" dy="2763" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-2" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-vPt7_FUP9xOXfKO9OSvj-1" style="rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-26" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-vPt7_FUP9xOXfKO9OSvj-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-25" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-vPt7_FUP9xOXfKO9OSvj-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Fifth Amendment Inverse Condemnation&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;The Claim: The SWAT team&#39;s physical destruction of the Nguyens&#39; home ($112,678 in damages) to execute a warrant was a public &quot;taking&quot; of private property for public use, requiring &quot;just compensation&quot; under the Fifth Amendment [JA 3]. The Defense: Tactical law enforcement damage is a non-compensable exercise of the state&#39;s emergency Police Power (or necessity), which operates as an exception to the Takings Clause [JA 9, 26, 32].&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Nguyens owned 3600 White Oaks Drive; the warrant identified Patterson at 3603, across the street. [JA 18–20]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;SWAT forced entry and deployed tear gas; doors, windows, the garage door, and fence were damaged. Remediation and repairs cost $112,678 and took almost 90 days. [JA 16, 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Council denied their property-damage claim; insurance also denied coverage. [JA 23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Wegner v. Milwaukee Mutual Insurance Co., 479 N.W.2d 38, 39–42 (Minn. 1991). SUPPORTIVE STATE-LAW ANALOGY. SWAT tear gas and flash-bangs damaged an innocent owner’s house; the city denied reimbursement. The court required compensation under Minnesota’s constitution. Similar damage, innocent owner, and denial; unlike this record, an armed suspect actually occupied the house. Its state “damaged” clause is broader than the federal text. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I5c3af345ff6411d9bf60c1d57ebc853e/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Baker v. City of McKinney, 84 F.4th 378, 383–88 (5th Cir. 2023). ADVERSE FEDERAL ANALOGY. Armored vehicles, explosives, and gas damaged an innocent owner’s home during a hostage emergency. No compensation where destruction was objectively necessary to prevent imminent harm. Distinguish the wrong address and disputed necessity here; Baker rejected a blanket police-power exception. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/Id3b7acb068a011eea76695209c33e2ad/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;UPDATE: Baker v. City of McKinney, No. 25-40396, 2026 WL 1453172, at *1, *3–4 (5th Cir. May 22, 2026) (unpublished), affirmed recovery under the Texas Constitution. It does not reverse the 2023 federal holding. Use only if the assignment permits post-record authorities. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/Ic724f4f0562611f19bdcd38b08cd9e81/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="4452.8" y="-414.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-vPt7_FUP9xOXfKO9OSvj-2" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Municipal Liability &amp;amp; Section 1983 Policy/Custom&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;The Claim: Mission City is liable under § 1983 because its City Council—the final policymaking body—voted to deny the Nguyens just compensation, thereby officially executing the municipal policy that completed the Fifth Amendment violation [JA 3–4, 28]. The Defense: There was no municipal policy to raid the wrong home, and the City cannot be held liable under a vicarious liability (respondeat superior) theory [JA 28, 32].&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Mission City is a municipal public corporation governed by a five-member Council empowered to make official City decisions; defendants admit these facts. [JA 1 ¶3; JA 7 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Nguyens filed their claim April 14, 2025. A May 24 letter reported that the Council voted to deny it. [JA 23 ¶14]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;This vote supports plaintiffs’ official-decision theory; the City argues there was no policy authorizing entry into the wrong house. [JA 28–29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Pembaur v. City of Cincinnati, 475 U.S. 469, 472–73, 480–85 (1986). Police forced entry into a doctor’s clinic to execute arrest process for employees after the county prosecutor ordered entry. A single decision by an authorized final policymaker can be policy. Similar official decision and forced entry; unlike the Council’s later denial, the prosecutor’s order preceded and directed the entry. Identify final authority over compensation and connect the decision to the claimed injury. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I618c8aa09c1f11d9bc61beebb95be672/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Knick v. Township of Scott, 588 U.S. 180, 185 (2019). A town required public access to a private cemetery. An unpaid taking creates an immediate § 1983 claim without a prior state compensation lawsuit. Timing analogy, not police-damage precedent: the later Council vote cannot simply be assumed to be the first moment of deprivation. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I06fa8dbd941811e9b22cbaf3cb96eb08/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="4305.6" y="-2208.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-4" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-3" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-14" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-13" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-16" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-15" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-24" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-1" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-23" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Is Mission City a person who, under color of any statute, ordinance, regulation, custom, or usage, of any State, subjected, or caused to be subjected, a citizen of the United States to the deprivation of any rights, privileges, or immunities secured by the Constitution and laws? Is P a party injured? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Mission City’s own SWAT officers entered and damaged the Nguyens’ home while executing an arrest warrant. [JA 12–16, 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Nguyens are U.S. citizens (admitted); repairs cost $112,678; the Council voted to deny their claim. [JA 1, 7, 23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;These facts support the elements; whether there was a taking and a causative municipal policy remains disputed. [JA 27–29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Hartsfield v. Lemacks, 50 F.3d 950, 951–56 (11th Cir. 1995), as amended June 14, 1995. Police used a battering ram at the wrong house despite a warrant naming another address. The leader lost qualified immunity because he made no reasonable verification effort; following officers retained it. Close wrong-address comparison, but this was a Fourth Amendment individual-liability ruling, not a municipal Fifth Amendment compensation holding. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I81219252918111d993e6d35cc61aab4a/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Pembaur, 475 U.S. at 480–85, supplies the separate municipal-policy analysis. Do not infer City liability merely because its officers performed the raid. Each § 1983 element and the specific constitutional deprivation must be established. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I618c8aa09c1f11d9bc61beebb95be672/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="3496.0" y="2070.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-6" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-3" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-5" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-8" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-3" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-7" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-12" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-3" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-11" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-3" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Is Mission City a person who&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Mission City is a municipal public corporation organized under Columbia law, with capacity to sue and be sued. [JA 1 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Defendants expressly admit paragraph 3. [JA 7 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Monell v. Department of Social Services, 436 U.S. 658, 660–62, 690–91 (1978). Female municipal employees challenged official maternity-leave policies. Local government bodies qualify as § 1983 persons, but employment alone does not create liability. Institutional analogy: Mission City’s admitted municipal status fits the defendant category; the underlying facts are employment, not a raid. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I6184263e9c1f11d9bc61beebb95be672/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="1398.4" y="4623.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-5" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;How have courts interpreted “person” in the Section 1983 context?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Relevant classification fact: Mission City is a municipal corporation, governed by its own five-member City Council. Defendants admit this status. [JA 1 ¶3; JA 7 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;How “person” is interpreted is a legal question; these facts establish the kind of defendant to which the rule would apply.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Monell, 436 U.S. at 690: “Congress did intend municipalities and other local government units to be included among those persons to whom § 1983 applies.” Apply to the admitted municipal corporation. No factually matching police case is needed to resolve this classification. Keep personhood separate from policy, causation, and a constitutional violation. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I6184263e9c1f11d9bc61beebb95be672/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="-920.0" y="6555.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-10" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-7" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-9" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-7" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;When does municipal liability attach under Section 1983?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Council has authority to make official City decisions. [JA 1 ¶3; admitted JA 7 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Council itself voted to deny the Nguyens’ submitted property-damage claim. [JA 23 ¶14]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Plaintiffs rely on this single official decision; the City disputes its causal connection to the alleged taking. [JA 28–29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Pembaur, 475 U.S. at 480: “municipal liability may be imposed for a single decision by municipal policymakers under appropriate circumstances.” The prosecutor’s instruction caused the forced clinic entry. Here, identify whether the Council finally decided compensation, and why that decision caused the uncompensated-taking injury. Part II-B’s discussion at 481–83 is a plurality. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I618c8aa09c1f11d9bc61beebb95be672/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Monell, 436 U.S. at 694, requires injury caused by execution of governmental policy or custom. A post-raid denial does not itself establish a policy directing wrong-address raids. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I6184263e9c1f11d9bc61beebb95be672/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="772.8000000000001" y="6555.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-9" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Under what circumstances may a property owner sue a municipality for just compensation when municipal police damage private property?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Owners’ home was forcibly entered by City SWAT; tear gas made it temporarily uninhabitable and required HAZMAT remediation. [JA 19, 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Repairs cost $112,678; insurance denied coverage and the Council denied their City claim. [JA 23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;These facts support uncompensated loss; whether police damage qualifies as a taking remains a legal dispute. [JA 27–28]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Steele v. City of Houston, 603 S.W.2d 786, 788–89, 791–93 (Tex. 1980). Police allegedly burned an innocent owner’s house to force out escaped prisoners. The court allowed a Texas constitutional destruction claim to proceed and rejected governmental immunity. Similar innocent ownership and police destruction; actual fugitives were inside. It required intentional destruction for public use and permitted a great-public-necessity defense: “Mere convenience will not suffice.” Id. at 792. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I3d7b267ae79311d9bf60c1d57ebc853e/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Hamen v. Hamlin County, 955 N.W.2d 336, 342–48, ¶¶ 4–14, 23–32 (S.D. 2021). Officers damaged a mobile home despite reports that the suspect had left; he was found outside. The court rejected the state takings claim under a police-power/public-use distinction. Particularly useful adverse analogy because absence of the suspect did not itself produce compensation. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/Ie2fe88206c9911eba660be4ce62361b9/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="257.6" y="8073.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-11" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Is this a situation where courts would extend liability to municipalities?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The denial came from the Council itself, not merely an individual officer: its vote was reported in the City’s May 24, 2025 letter. [JA 23 ¶14]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Council’s official-decision authority is admitted. [JA 1 ¶3; JA 7 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Supports plaintiffs’ theory of direct municipal action; it does not establish a City policy to raid wrong addresses. [JA 28–29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Pembaur, 475 U.S. at 480–85. A government’s own authorized decision can support liability even if it occurs once. The affirmative pre-entry order is stronger causal evidence than a later refusal to pay. Explain that difference rather than treating the cases as identical. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I618c8aa09c1f11d9bc61beebb95be672/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;City of Newport v. Fact Concerts, Inc., 453 U.S. 247, 250–53, 271 (1981). A city council canceled a concert license, producing civil-rights litigation. The council-action fact is analogous, but the holding relevant here is municipal immunity from § 1983 punitive damages; it does not establish that denial of a damage claim causes a taking. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I1d1a55069c9711d993e6d35cc61aab4a/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="2428.8" y="6555.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-13" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Was Mission City acting under the color of a statute, ordinance, regulation, custom, or usage of a State? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The police chief assigned Quick to execute a state arrest warrant. Quick commanded the City SWAT team and planned its deployment. [JA 12–15, 17]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;City officers carried out that operation, and the City Council later voted on the owners’ claim. [JA 16, 23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;These were exercises of governmental authority, supporting the under-color-of-law element.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;West v. Atkins, 487 U.S. 42, 49–57 (1988). A physician contracted to treat state prisoners acted under color of state law while performing that function. Functional analogy: Quick’s command of City SWAT and execution of a state warrant invoke official authority, even if exercised incorrectly. This proves the source of authority, not the City’s policy or liability. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I1786319b9c1f11d993e6d35cc61aab4a/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Hartsfield, 50 F.3d at 951–56, illustrates that a mistaken address during an official drug raid remains subject to § 1983 analysis. Its holding concerns individual Fourth Amendment liability, not an automatic municipal damages award. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I81219252918111d993e6d35cc61aab4a/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="3201.6000000000004" y="5175.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-18" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-15" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-17" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-22" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-15" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-21" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-15" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;If yes, in such action, did Mission City subject, or cause to be subjected, P to the deprivation of any rights, privileges, or immunities secured by the Constitution and laws? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;City SWAT breached the home, deployed tear gas, and damaged property; the Council later denied the owners’ claim. [JA 16, 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The resulting repairs cost $112,678. [JA 23 ¶13]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Supports plaintiffs’ claimed uncompensated deprivation; whether these acts violate the Fifth Amendment is contested. [JA 27–29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Hartsfield, 50 F.3d at 955–56. The leader had visited the correct house the previous day yet failed to verify the address; the homes were distinguishable. Compare Quick’s prior photograph and the houses’ differences. Distinguish the daylight, clearly marked numbers, and absence of exigency there from any supported nighttime or emergency facts here. It supports the Fourth Amendment route, not proof of a Fifth Amendment taking. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I81219252918111d993e6d35cc61aab4a/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Cedar Point Nursery v. Hassid, 594 U.S. 139, 159–61 (2021), distinguishes isolated tortious invasions from appropriations and recognizes traditional entry privileges. Explain why the particular damage is an appropriation, and whether the claimed privilege covered mistaken entry. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/Iab37444ed36711eb9531b93dba0730fb/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="5004.8" y="4692.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-20" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-17" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-19" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-17" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Did such action subject P to the deprivation of their 5th Amendment rights? In other words, did P have their private property taken for public use, without just compensation? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Private property: Kevin and Cindy owned the home. [JA 19 ¶3]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Public-purpose argument: City SWAT used the home in an operation intended to arrest a suspected fentanyl dealer. [JA 13, 15–16]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Uncompensated loss: $112,678 in repairs; Council voted to deny the claim. These support the taking theory, not a finding that a taking occurred. [JA 23; JA 27–28]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Wegner, 479 N.W.2d at 41–42, treated deliberate tear-gas damage while capturing a dangerous suspect as public use and required municipal compensation. Strong physical-damage and public-benefit analogy; its Minnesota constitutional holding cannot simply be substituted for federal law. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I5c3af345ff6411d9bf60c1d57ebc853e/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Steele, 603 S.W.2d at 791–93, required intentional destruction and public use. Distinguish an intentional decision to breach this particular house from a negligent choice of address. The court’s state-law analysis does not establish that every mistaken raid is a federal taking. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I3d7b267ae79311d9bf60c1d57ebc853e/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Baker, 84 F.4th at 388, supplies the opposing necessity analysis. The decisive comparison is the actual emergency and objective need for the particular destruction, not merely the amount of repair bills. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/Id3b7acb068a011eea76695209c33e2ad/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="4673.6" y="6279.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-19" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;See Issue 2. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Issue 2 facts: forced entry at 3600 although the warrant identified 3603; tear gas and damage to doors, windows, fence, and garage. [JA 16, 18, 22]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Home temporarily uninhabitable; HAZMAT remediation; repairs took almost 90 days and cost $112,678; Council denied claim. [JA 23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Apply Issue 2’s taking analysis to these facts.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Hamen, 955 N.W.2d at 342–48, ¶¶ 4–14, 23–32, is the adverse “suspect not inside” comparison. Officers had seen the suspect enter earlier but later received reports he had fled; the home was damaged anyway. Compare that prior evidentiary link with the Nguyens’ entirely wrong address. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/Ie2fe88206c9911eba660be4ce62361b9/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Wegner, 479 N.W.2d at 39–42, is the supportive tear-gas/home-remediation comparison. Use alongside Baker, not as proof that all SWAT damage is compensable. Both Hamen and Wegner decide their own state constitutional clauses. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I5c3af345ff6411d9bf60c1d57ebc853e/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="4563.2" y="7659.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-21" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Was Mission City the one subjecting or causing to be subjected? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;City SWAT physically caused the damage; Quick admits the team entered the wrong house. [JA 16; JA 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The Council itself voted to deny compensation. [JA 23 ¶14]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Plaintiffs connect that official denial to the unpaid taking; the City argues the later vote did not cause the original injury. [JA 28–29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Pembaur, 475 U.S. at 484–85, tied the forced entry to the county prosecutor’s final instruction. Here distinguish (1) the police decision causing physical damage and (2) the Council decision withholding compensation. Establish final policymaking authority for the activity actually challenged. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I618c8aa09c1f11d9bc61beebb95be672/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Knick, 588 U.S. at 185, places accrual at the unpaid taking, without first requiring a failed state compensation action. The later vote confirms refusal to pay, but a separate explanation is needed for why it satisfies Monell causation. Neither decision squarely holds that every post-incident refusal to reimburse satisfies Monell. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I06fa8dbd941811e9b22cbaf3cb96eb08/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="6329.6" y="6279.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-23" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Is P a citizen of the United States?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Kevin and Cindy allege they are U.S. citizens, married, and Columbia residents. [JA 1 ¶1]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Both defendants expressly admit paragraph 1. Citizenship is therefore admitted in the pleadings. [JA 7 ¶1]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;West, 487 U.S. at 48, states the deprivation and color-of-law elements. The Nguyens’ citizenship is admitted; no similar-fact citizenship case is necessary. Section 1983 also protects “other person[s] within the jurisdiction thereof,” so citizenship should not be framed as an absolute prerequisite. Concentrate research on the contested taking and municipal-policy issues. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I1786319b9c1f11d993e6d35cc61aab4a/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="5667.200000000001" y="3381.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-25" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;What relief is appropriate?&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Repair-cost evidence: $112,678, with almost 90 days of repairs and HAZMAT remediation. [JA 23 ¶¶12–13]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Requested relief: just compensation on Count II; damages according to proof, costs, and reasonable attorney’s fees on Count III. [JA 5]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;The repair total supports the requested amount; it does not itself decide the legally recoverable measure.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Baker, 2026 WL 1453172, at *1, *3–4 (unpublished), upheld $59,656.59 recovery for the same police raid under Texas law and rejected the City’s inadequately supported challenge to repair/replacement evidence. Close damages analogy; it does not adopt repair cost as an automatic federal measure. The decision also discusses election of remedies and avoiding double recovery under Texas law. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/Ic724f4f0562611f19bdcd38b08cd9e81/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Brown v. Legal Foundation of Washington, 538 U.S. 216, 235–37 (2003). In an IOLTA-interest taking, compensation turned on the owner’s pecuniary loss, not the government’s gain. Different facts, but useful to distinguish compensation from restitution. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I64fe1c3a9c9711d9bc61beebb95be672/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;City of Newport, 453 U.S. at 271, bars § 1983 punitive damages against the municipality. Document compensable repair/remediation loss and any separately supported loss of use; do not assume all requested relief follows automatically. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I1d1a55069c9711d993e6d35cc61aab4a/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="5409.6" y="2139.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-30" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-27" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-29" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-32" edge="1" parent="1" source="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-27" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-31" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-27" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Unjust Enrichment claim&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Officers entered and used the wrong home during the warrant operation, causing physical damage. [JA 16, 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Plaintiffs allege entry without consent, payment, or contract, and no intent to confer a gift. [JA 4 ¶¶21–24]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Claimed benefit: use/access without paying. This is plaintiffs’ theory; the City denies any recognizable benefit. [JA 29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Edwards v. Lee’s Administrator, 96 S.W.2d 1028, 1029–33 (Ky. 1936). A cave operator sold tours that traversed a neighbor’s underground property without permission. The owner recovered the share of net profits attributable to that use. Closer property-use analogy than a trade-secret case: unauthorized access can confer a recoverable benefit. Important difference: repeated willful commercial use produced proven profit; the City’s mistaken raid produced no comparable receipts. This is state private-party law, not a holding recognizing federal restitution against a city. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/Ic9177ac5ee6f11d983e7e9deff98dc6f/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Ward v. Board of County Commissioners of Love County, 253 U.S. 17, 23–24 (1920), required a county to refund unlawful coercively collected taxes. It supports restitution against a government that actually received value; show what distinct benefit Mission City received rather than relabeling $112,678 in owner loss. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I0741605c9cbc11d9bc61beebb95be672/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="8022.400000000001" y="-1311.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-29" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Is there any historical basis for recognizing this claim?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Factual analogy to trespass: Quick admits mistaken entry; officers forced entry and damaged the home. [JA 16, 22–23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Plaintiffs allege no consent and no gift. [JA 4 ¶¶21–24]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Historical recognition needs legal authority, not case facts. Counsel invoked older federal restitution cases and the Restatement, but that argument is not a holding. [JA 29]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Ward, 253 U.S. at 23–24, imposed a refund obligation for money coercively collected by a county from federally protected Indian allotments. Historical government-defendant example; unlike the raid, identifiable money passed to the government. It does not decide whether § 1983 displaces this pleaded equitable theory. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I0741605c9cbc11d9bc61beebb95be672/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Edwards, 96 S.W.2d at 1030–32, explains assumpsit, use and occupation, and an accounting for profits from unauthorized real-property use. Quote: “the unjust enrichment of the wrongdoer is the gist of the right to bring an action ex contractu.” Id. at 1031. Historical state-law analogy, not a federal municipal cause-of-action holding. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/Ic9177ac5ee6f11d983e7e9deff98dc6f/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="7360.0" y="207.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sc-MEIOTCxlJQS8ORqtbVFV-31" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;What relief is appropriate?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin:10px 10px 6px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting facts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:6px 0;padding-left:18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Plaintiffs request money equal to the cost of restoring the property to its pre-raid condition. [JA 5, prayer ¶4]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;Kevin reports $112,678 in repairs, including remediation after tear gas made the home temporarily uninhabitable. [JA 23]&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px;&quot;&gt;This proves claimed loss, not the value of the City’s alleged benefit; restitution’s proper measure remains to be established.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potentially relevant cases — Westlaw&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Edwards, 96 S.W.2d at 1031–33, measured the defendant’s benefit attributable to the property; it allowed a share of net cave profits, excluded hotel profits, and rejected gross-profit recovery. Quote: “They are limited to the benefits accruing to the appellants.” Id. at 1032. Identify a defensible use/access value or actual avoided expense. The City’s failure to pay a disputed damage claim does not itself establish enrichment equal to the repair bill. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/Ic9177ac5ee6f11d983e7e9deff98dc6f/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Contrast Brown, 538 U.S. at 235–37: just compensation concerns the owner’s loss. Restitution and compensation require different valuation evidence. Missing here: proof of a measurable City benefit, applicable restitution law and municipal defenses, and an explanation why § 1983 does not foreclose the particular independent claim. &lt;a href=&quot;https://1.next.westlaw.com/Document/I64fe1c3a9c9711d9bc61beebb95be672/View/FullText.html&quot;&gt;Westlaw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1050" width="600" x="8611.2" y="138.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="mcMStH24n5Qd2vchl8ZE" name="Oral Argument ">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" page="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-3" edge="1" parent="1" source="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-1" style="curved=1;rounded=0;curveGeometry=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-2" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-42" edge="1" parent="1" source="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-1" style="curved=1;rounded=0;curveGeometry=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-41" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Start&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Takings/ Just compensation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;1983&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Unjust enrichment&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="100" width="430" x="110" y="220" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-5" edge="1" parent="1" source="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-2" style="curved=1;rounded=0;curveGeometry=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-4" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-30" edge="1" parent="1" source="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-2" style="curved=1;rounded=0;curveGeometry=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-29" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-36" edge="1" parent="1" source="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-2" style="curved=1;rounded=0;curveGeometry=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-35" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-2" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;Takings/ Just compensation&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- establish there is a substantive right to compensation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;Established by:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;Knick &amp;amp; 5th — (1)&amp;nbsp;Timing: The right arises immediately upon an uncompensated taking. Id. at 192.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;(2) T&lt;/span&gt;he compensation right rests on the Fifth Amendment. Id. at 190–91.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;(3) &lt;/span&gt;Ending the taking does not erase compensation owed for its duration. Id. at 192–93.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&quot;The Framers meant to prohibit the Federal Government from taking property without paying for it.&quot; 2019 Justice Roberts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="720" x="-1580" y="410" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-7" edge="1" parent="1" source="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-4" style="curved=1;rounded=0;curveGeometry=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-6" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-9" edge="1" parent="1" source="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-4" style="curved=1;rounded=0;curveGeometry=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-8" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-11" edge="1" parent="1" source="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-4" style="curved=1;rounded=0;curveGeometry=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-10" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-15" edge="1" parent="1" source="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-4" style="curved=1;rounded=0;curveGeometry=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-14" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-17" edge="1" parent="1" source="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-4" style="curved=1;rounded=0;curveGeometry=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-16" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-21" edge="1" parent="1" source="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-4" style="curved=1;rounded=0;curveGeometry=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-20" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-4" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;1983 provides the right to action&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;- establish 1983 claim then municipal liability (Monel claim)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;(a) An underlying violation of a federal right. - showed in takings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;(b) &lt;/span&gt;A municipal policy or custom- main argument about the ruling &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;(c) Causation - causation tied in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="450" x="280" y="480" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="asF2fj-k3maLoz7lA8SP-2" edge="1" parent="1" source="t4PtQhD98tMtrIm2gATw-6" style="curved=1;rounded=0;curveGeometry=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;defaultLabelBackgroundColor=gap;" target="asF2fj-k3maLoz7lA8SP-1" value="">
